<!-- driver-lint:start -->
## Camera/GDC engineering and commit gate

Read `driver_lint/CLAUDE.md` and the active project profile in
`driver_lint/config/policy.json` before editing scoped drivers. Common
lifecycle/buffer/PM/API responsibilities and HW-specific implementations are
separate. Family and IP versions are independent; intended HW migrations update
the project profile and HW/build code with evidence.

Use the installed agent hook/plugin for edit feedback. Before finishing, run
`python3 driver_lint/lint.py scan`. In Git projects the installed pre-commit hook
runs `python3 driver_lint/scripts/commit_gate.py`: it checks staged configuration,
build contracts and source blobs, including partial staging. Errors or inability
to verify reject the commit. Let the hook run on every commit; repair failures
without disabling the hook or weakening common policy. CI checks committed
changes against the review base and must be required for merge.

Include warnings, selected profile, build/KUnit/HW results and pending validation
in the review. A passing lint does not establish correct HW behavior. This release
root currently uses a source snapshot until it is hosted in an actual Git project.
<!-- driver-lint:end -->
